meta {
  name: 24 Outsource Sample
  type: http
  seq: 24
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/accession/order-samples/{{sampleId}}/outsource
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "outsourceCenterId": "{{outsourceCenterId}}",
    "sendDate": "2026-10-08",
    "sendTime": "14:30",
    "logisticsType": "Courier",
    "outsourceStatus": "Dispatched",
    "notes": "Sent to third-party lab"
  }
}

tests {
  test("transition applied (or rejected by the state machine)", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.be.oneOf([200, 201, 404, 422]);
  });
}

docs {
  Outsource — **Accepted → Outsourced**, creating an OUTSOURCE `SampleTransfer`.

  `outsourceCenterId` is **optional at this step**: omit it to mark the sample
  Outsourced now and assign the center later via **Assign Center**
  (`POST /accession/transfers/:id/assign-center`) — mirroring the Internal Send
  flow whose station is likewise optional-then-assignable. When supplied it must
  reference an existing `OutsourceCenter` in the caller's tenant (validated → 404
  `ACCESSION_OUTSOURCE_CENTER_NOT_FOUND` if missing); when omitted the transfer is
  created with a null center.

  `sendDate`/`sendTime` are optional (the UI pre-fills them with "now"); `sendDate`
  defaults to the current time server-side when absent. Third-party labs don't use
  Kalnostic, so tracking is **manual** via `outsourceStatus` (CR-3). Bulk:
  `POST /accession/order-samples/bulk/outsource`.

  > To outsource *with* a center, set `{{outsourceCenterId}}` from the Outsource
  > Centers folder first; otherwise drop that body field to test the assign-later
  > flow.

  **Report must be untouched.** Like a Send to another branch, Outsource is refused (422
  `SAMPLE_SEND_BLOCKED`) when a report the sample serves has already been worked on: past
  Pending, or holding result values, notes, attachments, overall results or a lock. The
  message says why: "The report for this test has already been worked on (results, notes
  or attachments exist, or it is past Pending), so the sample cannot be outsourced." A group
  call with `skipInvalid: true` skips that sample with the same reason (code and sentence
  under `skipped`) and sends the others; without it the whole call is refused, even with
  `force`. The check is made at hand-over only: once out, the sending branch can keep
  working the report.

  **Center and logistics before it moves.** Both `outsourceCenterId` and `logisticsType` stay optional
  here (assign later with Assign Center), but until BOTH are set the transfer can not be Picked Up, and until the center
  is set it can not be Received or Accepted (422 `TRANSFER_OUTSOURCE_NOT_ASSIGNED`). In the In-House Orders list the
  sample reads "Outsourced – Not assigned" (or "Logistics needed" / "Center needed" when only one is missing) until then, then "Outsourced – In-Transit / Picked Up / Received / Accepted /
  Repeated / Rejected" as the Outsource tab moves the transfer.
}
